tsql: support MERGE ... OUTPUT (result-set form)

Builds on babelfishpg_tsql.enable_tsql_merge (#4928, #4982). Adds the OUTPUT clause for MERGE,
which is what Entity Framework Core's SQL Server provider emits for batched inserts:

    MERGE [T] USING (VALUES ...) AS i ([c], _Position) ON 1=0
    WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT ([c]) VALUES (i.[c]) OUTPUT INSERTED.[Id], i._Position;

PostgreSQL 18 already has MERGE ... RETURNING with old / new row references and merge_action(),
so the OUTPUT list becomes the RETURNING list:

  - backend grammar: new tsql_MergeOutputStmt (MERGE ... tsql_output_clause) producing a MergeStmt
    with a returningClause; inserted.<c> / deleted.<c> are renamed to new.<c> / old.<c>
    (NULL for the missing side of an INSERT / DELETE action, as in SQL Server). No engine change.
  - ANTLR layer: $action => merge_action(). The OUTPUT keyword and the pseudo-tables are left as
    T-SQL because the rewritten text is parsed by ANTLR a second time (e.g. CREATE PROCEDURE
    bodies), so every rewrite has to stay valid T-SQL.
  - executor: report CMD_MERGE with RETURNING (SPI_OK_MERGE_RETURNING) like the other DML forms.
  - OUTPUT ... INTO stays unsupported, now with its own message ("MERGE with OUTPUT INTO").

Known differences from SQL Server: @@ROWCOUNT is 0 after any DML that returns OUTPUT rows (as for
INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE ... OUTPUT in Babelfish today); TOP in MERGE is still unsupported.

